## Architecture

```
src/
├── main.ts                       ← hybrid HTTP + microservice bootstrap (NestFactory.create + connectMicroservice)
├── app.module.ts
├── config/
│   └── app.config.ts
└── <moduleName>/
    ├── <moduleName>.controller.ts ← @MessagePattern / @EventPattern handlers for RPC and events
    └── <moduleName>.module.ts
```

The app starts **two listeners** on a single process:
1. An HTTP server (Express/Fastify) on `PORT` (default 3000)
2. A microservice transport listener on `MICROSERVICE_PORT` (default 3001)

Message handlers in controllers respond to remote procedure calls (`@MessagePattern`) and handle
asynchronous events (`@EventPattern`). External services communicate with this microservice
by connecting a `ClientProxy` over the configured transport (TCP, Redis, Kafka, RabbitMQ, NATS, or gRPC).

